HW-MAINS-CYCLE n=1 utc=2026-09-21T03:35Z cause=INSTRUCTED-PROBE not=hardware-fault
  what: a drive-map probe (VOL C:;VOL D:;VOL E:;VOL F:) hit the empty optical
        drive, raised DOS critical error CDR101, and blocked the machine at
        "Abort, Retry, Fail?" with no automated way to answer it.
  then: PS/2 link stopped carrying keystrokes (verify_input false; a typed 'F'
        did not reach the prompt), so no warm reboot was possible.
  attribution: NOT the documented post-FTP keyboard hang, although
        verify_input produced that fault's exact signature. The screenshot
        showed the harness's own "CD C:\FSTEST" and "PRUN.BAT" had typed and
        executed, so the input path was alive when the probe started. Filing
        this under the hardware fault would have corrupted the power log as
        evidence about the machine.
  recovery: one mains cycle. After: power 24,195 mW, verify_input true, full
        boot sequence verified by capture through "[PGSB] ready."
  prevention: read the drive map from the MSCDEX boot banner, which the
        capture channel already carries, instead of probing removable media.
