# READING (2026-09-24, dosags-worker; see PLAN.md and run-hw.sh be42cfa0): the STOPPED-second-failure entries for
# HW-MMD-0 and HANGTEST1/2/3 are a HARNESS NAMING BUG, not target hangs -- the engine writes the manifest as the tag
# uppercased, [A-Z0-9_] only, 8 chars (HW-MMD-0 -> HWMMD0.LOG, HANGTEST1..3 -> HANGTEST.LOG), run-hw asked for
# <TAG>.LOG verbatim, so every collection came back not-ok and was read as the dead link. HWMMD0.LOG and
# HANGTEST.LOG were found on C:\DOSAGS. S2S1/S2S2 (4-char tags) are NOT explained by this; no S2S manifest is on
# the target. C1A2, RBB1, RH090233, FIVE1 tags are name-safe, not explained either.
